WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:01.820
Jim Corbett [LSU Athletic Director].

2
00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:04.560
When I became President [of LSU], I told Jim, I said, “Now I want to tell you something.

3
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:11.840
You run that Athletic Department,” but I said, “It sure better be run right, because,” I said, “You know, General [Troy H.] Middleton,

4
00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:18.040
I remember him making a statement that if LSU is ever involved in anything that isn’t totally and completely legal,

5
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:21.040
that whoever the coach is involved, I’m going to fire him off the next day.”

6
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.500
And I said, “I’ll do the same thing.”

7
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.720
So we didn’t set up a search committee to find a . . . find a head football coach.

8
00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:31.000
One Sunday morning, down when I lived on Brame Drive [in Baton Rouge],

9
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.220
shortly after I had become . . . had been inaugurated . . . Well, it was before I was inaugurated.

10
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:43.420
Jim Corbett came down to the house and he said, “John . . .” And now in the meantime, [Paul] Dietzel had gone to West Point.

11
00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:49.240
He’d hauled off everybody he could haul off with him except Charlie McClendon and maybe one or two other people.

12
00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:54.673
And Jim came to me and he said, “John,” he said, “Let’s make Charlie Mac head football coach.”

13
00:00:54.673 --> 00:00:56.540
He said, “I’ve struggled with this.”

14
00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:58.740
And I said, “Jim, that’s fine.”

15
00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:05.180
So at this point we got on the phone from the kitchen and my bedroom and merely called John Doles [John J. Doles, Sr.],

16
00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:12.640
who was chairman of the [LSU] Board [of Supervisors] at that time, and said, “John, we want to make Charlie Mac our football coach.

17
00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.940
But, we got a problem: Kentucky wants him also.

18
00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:22.880
So we don’t want to do anything without the Board’s knowing about this thing.”

19
00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.640
John said to me, he said, “John, you all go ahead.”

20
00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:27.640
He said, “I know whatever you all do, is all right with the Board.”

21
00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.580
But he said, “I’ll call the Board, too.”

22
00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:38.020
Well, of course we get a hold of Charlie Mac and sure enough Kentucky’s board is meeting that afternoon!

23
00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:40.420
Well, I knew Frank Dickey, President of the University of Kentucky.

24
00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:44.340
I knew him well, so I called him, and I said, “You call him out of the meeting.”

25
00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:50.900
And I said, “Frank, are you all considering Charlie Mac as your new head football coach?”

26
00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:52.060
He said, “John, we sure are.”

27
00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:55.620
And I said, “Well, we’re going to try to keep him from going.

28
00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:56.940
I think we would like to keep him here.”

29
00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:00.560
He said, “Well, that’s fine with us,” but I said . . . He said,

30
00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.100
“But he is . . . will probably be elected up here.”

31
00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:12.480
So we called Charlie Mac, and he came over to the house and we . . . never forget this, back in my bedroom,

32
00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:18.240
we were sitting there on the edge of the bed and chair and here is Charlie Mac,

33
00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:24.460
who all of the sudden realizes, he is not stupid, he knows he is being considered in Kentucky.

34
00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:27.300
And all of a sudden here’s this LSU thing.

35
00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:31.640
And it was not easy to convince him to come to LSU.

36
00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:38.780
A graduate of University of Kentucky, he felt a real strong desire to go back there.

37
00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:43.940
Well, I don’t . . . I’ve forgotten how Jim and I did it, but anyhow Charlie Mac finally said, “Well, all right, I’ll do it.”

38
00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:47.320
But I said, “Well, first, let’s get your wife down here.”

39
00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:56.980
So we called Dorothy Faye [McClendon] and she came back to our house and in the meantime my wife was off in the kitchen minding her business and wondering what in the heck was going on back in the kitchen . . . back in the bedroom,

40
00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:00.200
except she knew we were trying to hire Charlie McClendon.

41
00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:05.760
And Dorothy Faye came in and . . . By the way, whatever history shows,

42
00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:11.920
I hope they show that she’s one of the loveliest, prettiest, sweetest people that has ever been connected with LSU.

43
00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:12.940
She is a marvelous lady.

44
00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:16.920
Well, I told her, I said, “Dorothy Faye,

45
00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:22.880
we want Charlie Mac to become football coach and we just . . . he has about agreed to do it,

46
00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:26.440
but we want your total approval of it also.”

47
00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:28.900
And she said, “Well . . .” She always called me Dr. John,

48
00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:32.960
and she said, “Dr. John, whatever you all want it is fine with me.”

49
00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:39.860
So at this point, we shook hands with Charlie Mac, and said, “Go on about your business, keep your mouth shut, give us a few minutes.”

50
00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:45.780
I got on the phone in the kitchen, called John Doles and told him that we had hired McClendon,

51
00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:49.160
and we would like to poll the Board to approve our decision.

52
00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:55.720
And from the kitchen phone we telephoned every member of the LSU Board and they said, “Well, sure that’s great!”

53
00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:57.020
And that was it, and that was it.

54
00:03:57.020 --> 00:04:04.060
Then, two hours later Jim Corbett called [Vesta] “Bud” Montet, I believe, down at the [Advocate] newspaper and had a short press conference.

55
00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:05.740
Charlie Mac was coach.
